    {
      "id": "p0242-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In basketball, it's humiliating if someone performs a slam dunk over you. Thus the phrase \"to be dunked on\" is a humorous way of saying \"you've been completely dominated\" or \"you're nothing to me\". As it's a relatively new slang phrase and isn't often seen in video games, this surprise appearance adds extra humor to the line.",
        "raw": "In basketball, it's humiliating if someone performs a slam dunk over you.\nThus the phrase \"to be dunked on\" is a humorous way of saying \"you've been\ncompletely dominated\" or \"you're nothing to me\". As it's a relatively new slang\nphrase and isn't often seen in video games, this surprise appearance adds extra\nhumor to the line.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29475395,
          0.38376429,
          0.89622212,
          0.47036429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29221845,
          0.38305,
          0.90273764,
          0.47143571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          15,
          16,
          17,
          18,
          19
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "篮球比赛中，被人隔着自己扣篮很丢脸。因此，“be dunked on”（被隔扣）也成了调侃人的说法，意思是“你被彻底碾压了”或“你在我眼里什么也不是”。这句俚语比较新，在游戏里又不常见，突然冒出来就更好笑了。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
